_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 101
---
order: 101
---
short_label: X.101
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: The square on the straight line which produces with a rational area a medial whole, if applied to a rational straight line, produces as breadth a fifth apotome.
----
proof:

Let {AB} be the straight line which produces with a rational area a medial whole, and {CD} a rational straight line, and to {CD} let {CE|CEh} be applied equal to the square on {AB} and producing {CF} as breadth.

I say that {CF} is a fifth apotome.

Let {BG|GB} be the annex to {AB}. Then {AG} and {GB} are straight lines incommensurable in square which make the sum of the squares on them medial but twice the rectangle contained by them rational. [!just X.77]

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="370" height="190" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="X.101 diagram" src="propX101.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Joyce's figure: AB with its annex BG on the line AG, the rational line
    // CD, and on it CE (DCFE) equal to the square on AB, overlaid by FKHE
    // (completing CH, the square on AG) and HKML (KL, the square on GB), all
    // random-faced, with N bisecting FM and the parallel NO.
    // Added, all hidden at rest: solid twins ABs, GBs (initiallyHidden) so
    // AB stands alone before G and the annex is produced from B; transparent
    // targets AB, GB, CF, CK, KM, CM, FM, NM, EF, ML (;0;0;0); faceless,
    // strokeless targets CEh (twin of the random-faced DCFE, which would be
    // raised over its neighbours when lit, #140), CHh, KLh, CLh, FLh, FOh,
    // NLh for the rectangles the text names, reached with the display
    // override ({CE|CEh}). No angle is called right, so no markers.
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): A, B, G, C, D (line sliders)
    // and the offscreen frees. C and D arrive with "and CD a rational
    // straight line", G with the annex, so all three are deferred. F, E, K,
    // H, M, L, N, O are derived and listed per slide.
    var GIVEN = ["A","B","AB","ABs"];
    var RAT   = GIVEN.concat(["C","D","CD"]);
    var APPL  = RAT.concat(["F","E","DCFE","CEh","CF"]);
    var ANNEX = APPL.concat(["G","GB","GBs"]);
    var WHOLE = ANNEX.concat(["AG"]);
    var SQS   = WHOLE.concat(["K","H","M","L","FKHE","HKML","CHh","KLh","CLh","CK","KM","CM"]);
    var REM   = SQS.concat(["FLh","FM","ML"]);
    var ALL   = REM.concat(["N","O","NO","FOh","NLh","EF","NM"]);
