            { text: "Then {AG} and {GB} are straight lines incommensurable in square",
              visible: WHOLE,
              highlighted: ["AG","GB"] },
            { text: "which make the sum of the squares on them medial but twice the rectangle contained by them rational.",
              visible: WHOLE,
              highlighted: ["AG","GB"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AB makes with a rational area a medial whole", ref: "X.77" }] },
            { text: "To {CD} apply {CH|CHh} equal to the square on {AG}, and {KL|KLh} equal to the square on {GB}.",
              visible: SQS,
              highlighted: ["CD","AG","GB"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "FKHE", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill },
                  { elem: "HKML", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill } ] } },
            { text: "Then the whole {CL|CLh} equals the sum of the squares on {AG} and {GB}.",
              visible: SQS,
              highlighted: ["CLh","AG","GB"] },
            { text: "But the sum of the squares on {AG} and {GB} together is medial, therefore {CL|CLh} is medial.",
              visible: SQS,
              highlighted: ["AG","GB","CLh"] },
            { text: "And it is applied to the rational straight line {CD} producing {CM} as breadth,",
              visible: SQS,
              highlighted: ["CLh","CD","CM"] },
            { text: "therefore {CM} is rational and incommensurable with {CD}.",
              visible: SQS,
              highlighted: ["CM","CD"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "CM rational, incommensurable with CD", ref: "X.22" }] },
            { text: "Since the whole {CL|CLh} equals the sum of the squares on {AG} and {GB},",
              visible: SQS,
              highlighted: ["CLh","AG","GB"] },
            { text: "and, in these, {CE|CEh} equals the square on {AB},",
              visible: SQS,
              highlighted: ["CEh","AB"] },
            { text: "therefore the remainder {FL|FLh} equals twice the rectangle {AG} by {GB}.",
              visible: REM,
              highlighted: ["FLh","AG","GB"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AG² + GB² = 2 AG·GB + AB²", ref: "II.7" }] },
            { text: "Bisect {FM} at {N}, and draw {NO} through {N} parallel to either of the straight lines {CD} or {ML}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FM","CD","ML"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "N",  name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "NO", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] } },
            { text: "Then each of the rectangles {FO|FOh} and {NL|NLh} equals the rectangle {AG} by {GB}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FOh","NLh","AG","GB"] },
            { text: "And, since twice the rectangle {AG} by {GB} is rational and equal to {FL|FLh}, therefore {FL|FLh} is rational.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AG","GB","FLh"] },
            { text: "And it is applied to the rational straight line {EF} producing {FM} as breadth,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FLh","EF","FM"] },
            { text: "therefore {FM} is rational and commensurable in length with {CD}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FM","CD"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "FM rational, commensurable with CD", ref: "X.20" }] },
            { text: "Now, since {CL|CLh} is medial, and {FL|FLh} rational, therefore {CL|CLh} is incommensurable with {FL|FLh}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CLh","FLh"] },
            { text: "But {CL|CLh} is to {FL|FLh} as {CM} is to {MF|FM},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CLh","FLh","CM","FM"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "CL : FL = CM : MF", ref: "VI.1" }] },
            { text: "therefore {CM} is incommensurable in length with {MF|FM}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CM","FM"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "CM, MF incommensurable", ref: "X.11" }] },
            { text: "And both are rational, therefore {CM} and {MF|FM} are rational straight lines commensurable in square only.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CM","FM"] },
            { text: "Therefore {CF} is an apotome.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CF"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "CF an apotome", ref: "X.73" }] },
            { text: "I say next that it is also a fifth apotome.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CF"] },
            { text: "We can prove similarly that the rectangle {CK} by {KM} equals the square on {NM},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CK","KM","NM"] },
            { text: "that is, the fourth part of the square on {FM}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["NM","FM"] },
            { text: "And, since the square on {AG} is incommensurable with the square on {GB},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AG","GB"] },
            { text: "while the square on {AG} equals {CH|CHh}, and the square on {GB} equals {KL|KLh},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AG","CHh","GB","KLh"] },
            { text: "therefore {CH|CHh} is incommensurable with {KL|KLh}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CHh","KLh"] },
            { text: "But {CH|CHh} is to {KL|KLh} as {CK} is to {KM},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CHh","KLh","CK","KM"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "CH : KL = CK : KM", ref: "VI.1" }] },
            { text: "therefore {CK} is incommensurable in length with {KM}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CK","KM"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "CK, KM incommensurable", ref: "X.11" }] },
            { text: "Since {CM} and {MF|FM} are two unequal straight lines,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CM","FM"] },
            { text: "and a parallelogram equal to the fourth part of the square on {FM} and deficient by a square figure",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FM","CK","KM"] },
            { text: "has been applied to {CM}, and divides it into incommensurable parts,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CM","CK","KM"] },
            { text: "therefore the square on {CM} is greater than the square on {MF|FM}",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CM","FM"] },
            { text: "by the square on a straight line incommensurable with {CM}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CM"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "CM² − MF² incommensurable with CM", ref: "X.18" }] },
            { text: "And the annex {FM} is commensurable with the rational straight line {CD} set out,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FM","CD"] },
            { text: "therefore {CF} is a fifth apotome.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CF"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "CF a fifth apotome", ref: "X.Def.III.5" }] },
            { text: "Therefore, the square on the straight line which produces with a rational area a medial whole,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB"] },
            { text: "if applied to a rational straight line, produces as breadth a fifth apotome.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CD","CEh","CF"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.D." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "X.101") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "II.7":        "/elements/books/bookII/propositions/propII7/",
        "VI.1":        "/elements/books/bookVI/propositions/propVI1/",
        "X.11":        "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX11/",
        "X.18":        "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX18/",
        "X.20":        "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX20/",
        "X.22":        "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX22/",
        "X.73":        "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX73/",
        "X.77":        "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX77/",
        "X.Def.III.5": "/elements/books/bookX/definitions/defX.III.5/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

To {CD} apply {CH|CHh} equal to the square on {AG}, and {KL|KLh} equal to the square on {GB}. Then the whole {CL|CLh} equals the sum of the squares on {AG} and {GB}.

But the sum of the squares on {AG} and {GB} together is medial, therefore {CL|CLh} is medial.

And it is applied to the rational straight line {CD} producing {CM} as breadth, therefore {CM} is rational and incommensurable with {CD}. [!just X.22]

Since the whole {CL|CLh} equals the sum of the squares on {AG} and {GB}, and, in these, {CE|CEh} equals the square on {AB}, therefore the remainder {FL|FLh} equals twice the rectangle {AG} by {GB}. [!just II.7]

Bisect {FM} at {N}, and draw {NO} through {N} parallel to either of the straight lines {CD} or {ML}. Then each of the rectangles {FO|FOh} and {NL|NLh} equals the rectangle {AG} by {GB}.

And, since twice the rectangle {AG} by {GB} is rational and equal to {FL|FLh}, therefore {FL|FLh} is rational.

And it is applied to the rational straight line {EF} producing {FM} as breadth, therefore {FM} is rational and commensurable in length with {CD}. [!just X.20]

Now, since {CL|CLh} is medial, and {FL|FLh} rational, therefore {CL|CLh} is incommensurable with {FL|FLh}.

But {CL|CLh} is to {FL|FLh} as {CM} is to {MF|FM}, therefore {CM} is incommensurable in length with {MF|FM}. [!just VI.1, X.11]

And both are rational, therefore {CM} and {MF|FM} are rational straight lines commensurable in square only. Therefore {CF} is an apotome. [!just X.73]

I say next that it is also a fifth apotome.

We can prove similarly that the rectangle {CK} by {KM} equals the square on {NM}, that is, the fourth part of the square on {FM}.

And, since the square on {AG} is incommensurable with the square on {GB}, while the square on {AG} equals {CH|CHh}, and the square on {GB} equals {KL|KLh}, therefore {CH|CHh} is incommensurable with {KL|KLh}.

But {CH|CHh} is to {KL|KLh} as {CK} is to {KM}, therefore {CK} is incommensurable in length with {KM}. [!just VI.1, X.11]

Since {CM} and {MF|FM} are two unequal straight lines, and a parallelogram equal to the fourth part of the square on {FM} and deficient by a square figure has been applied to {CM}, and divides it into incommensurable parts, therefore the square on {CM} is greater than the square on {MF|FM} by the square on a straight line incommensurable with {CM}. [!just X.18]

And the annex {FM} is commensurable with the rational straight line {CD} set out, therefore {CF} is a fifth apotome. [!just X.Def.III.5]

Therefore, *the square on the straight line which produces with a rational area a medial whole, if applied to a rational straight line, produces as breadth a fifth apotome.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
